Done in lap session S6 (git `846e13d`).

The stale badge's refresh now refreshes **that document from its own source**, never the store:
- **URL** locator → fetched again, after the same "Fetch <host>?" consent adding a URL asks for (the only network request Knowledge makes);
- **file path** → read again;
- the text is re-filed through `kb add` under the document's title, collection, locator, mime and meta, so kb's hash comparison decides: **unchanged** (only the fetch date moves) or **re-indexed**;
- **inline** content (handed over by an agent), a **moved** file, or a **declined** fetch say plainly why nothing happened.

The outcome is announced every time — unchanged and re-indexed look identical on the page otherwise.

Tests: the pure plan and wording (`src/refresh.ts`), plus a test against the **real kb binary** with a stand-in `vscode`: changed file re-indexed keeping title/collection/meta, unchanged only moves its date, moved file and inline content refused, declined fetch files nothing. index-vscode 90/91 (only T-14), combined build and check green.

Not verified in a real VS Code window; a URL refresh has not been run against a live site (the test only covers declining).

